      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **Approved** — All checks pass.\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** ✅ Correctly drops logs from any non-yielding context by checking `!k_can_yield()`, preventing mutex lock attempts in restricted contexts (e.g., idle thread, IRQ-disabled blocks).\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Idiomatically delegates non-yielding context detection to the Zephyr kernel (`k_can_yield()`).\n*   **Code Simplicity:** ✅ Minimal and direct early return.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ Uses clean standard Zephyr APIs (`irq_lock`, `irq_unlock`, `k_can_yield`) and straightforward assertions.\n*   **Security:** ✅ No new security implications.\n*   **Testing:** ✅ Adds a comprehensive unit test (`test_buf_dropped_logs_irq_lock`) simulating a non-yielding context with `irq_lock()` and validating that the payload is dropped and the `dropped_logs_isr` counter increments correctly.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ Size: S (+28, -3). The CL is a small, single logical change focused exclusively on preventing non-yielding contexts from acquiring the console mutex.\n*   **Commit Message:** ✅ The commit message accurately reflects the behavioral change, provides clear rationale, and strictly adheres to ChromiumOS formatting styles (`BUG\u003db:...` and `TEST\u003d...`).\n\n[[trajectory](https://goto.corp.google.com/traj/7d85e8f3-11ef-4872-aab0-ed8a9165af26)]",
