      "side": 1,
      "message": "[`k_can_yield()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/kernel/thread.c;l\u003d1897-1901;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) also returns false during `PRE_KERNEL_1` and `PRE_KERNEL_2` (both `k_is_pre_kernel()` and `!arch_cpu_irqs_are_enabled()` are true in [`z_cstart()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/kernel/init.c;l\u003d535-588;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745)).\n\nHowever, [`init_ec_console()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console.c;l\u003d306-314;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) and [`init_ec_shell()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console.c;l\u003d352-379;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) run at `PRE_KERNEL_1` specifically so `PRE_KERNEL_2` init functions can log. For example, [`panic_data_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d372-442;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) runs at `PRE_KERNEL_2` with `/* Initialize panic data after reset flags and console are ready. */` and logs `\"Watchdog Reset Detected\"` and `\"New Panic Detected: ...\"`.\n\nChecking `!k_can_yield()` here will cause all `PRE_KERNEL` console output (such as `LOG_*` under `CONFIG_LOG_MODE_MINIMAL\u003dy` or direct [`cprints()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console.c;l\u003d662;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745)/[`cputs()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console.c;l\u003d588;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) calls) to be dropped from the AP console buffer and counted under `dropped_logs_isr` (and under `CONFIG_LOG_MODE_MINIMAL\u003dy`, [`zephyr_shim_console_out()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console.c;l\u003d322-332;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) calls `console_buf_notify_chars()` 1 byte at a time, incrementing `dropped_logs_isr` once per character).\n\n(Unit tests don\u0027t catch this because [`zephyr/test/drivers/panic`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/drivers/panic/src/panic.c;l\u003d75-76;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) and [`zephyr/test/jump_data`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/jump_data/src/main.c;l\u003d423-435;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) populate reset flags/panic data and call `panic_data_init()` directly from a post-kernel Ztest thread where `k_can_yield()` is true—and don\u0027t inspect [`uart_console_read_buffer()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d286;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745)—while [`zephyr/test/drivers/console_buffer`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/drivers/console_buffer/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d131-135;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) has no `PRE_KERNEL` producer and flushes the buffer at the start of each test.)",
