      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking across the full stack (https://crrev.com/c/8607949 – https://crrev.com/c/8607952), is there a simpler approach that addresses the root cause without dropping logs in non-yielding contexts?\n\n### Why `console_buf_notify_chars()` fails when `!k_can_yield()`\nThere are only two things inside [`console_buf_notify_chars()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d115-171;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) that are unsafe when [`!k_can_yield()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/kernel/thread.c;l\u003d1897-1901;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745):\n1. **[`console_write_lock`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d113;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) is a `k_mutex` instead of a `k_spinlock`**:\n   - A `k_mutex` cannot be locked in an ISR, can trigger `z_reschedule()` on unlock if acquired from the idle thread while interrupts are enabled, and acquires Zephyr\u0027s global `mutex_lock` spinlock in [`z_impl_k_mutex_lock()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/kernel/mutex.c;l\u003d202-253;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) (which panics if an assertion/log fires while the kernel is already inside a `k_mutex` call).\n   - Meanwhile, the buffer manipulations in [`console_buf_notify_chars()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d115-171;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745), [`uart_console_read_buffer_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d173-200;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745), and [`uart_console_read_buffer()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d286-338;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) are just in-memory ring-buffer copies and index updates.\n2. **[`console_log_notify_host()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d51-77;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) is called inside `console_buf_notify_chars()`**:\n   - `et171` enables [`CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_CONSOLE_EVENT\u003dy`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/et171/prj.conf;l\u003d105;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745).\n   - When `console_buf_notify_chars()` sees `\u0027\\n\u0027`, [`console_log_notify_host()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d74;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) calls [`host_set_single_event(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS)`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/host_event_commands.c;l\u003d349-355;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) -\u003e [`activate_mkbp_with_events()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/mkbp_event.c;l\u003d251-286;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745), which takes a **blocking** mutex (`k_mutex_lock(\u0026state.lock, K_FOREVER)`) and schedules a delayed work item (`hook_call_deferred()`). That is what actually blocks or fails during `PRE_KERNEL`, spinlocks, or ISRs.\n\n### Suggested Approach: Spinlock for `console_buf` + `k_can_yield()` only on `console_log_notify_host()`\nNote that https://crrev.com/c/8478812 (*\"console_buffer: Protect the buffer with a spinlock\"*) already implements this pattern in `console_buffer.c`:\n1. Replace `K_MUTEX_DEFINE(console_write_lock)` with `static struct k_spinlock console_lock;` (moving [`host_clear_events()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d194;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) before `k_spin_lock(\u0026console_lock)` in [`uart_console_read_buffer_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d173-200;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745), and moving [`format_dropped_logs_msg()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d213-223;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) before `k_spin_lock(\u0026console_lock)` in [`uart_console_read_buffer()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d286-338;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) since its override in [`pw_log_zephyr_tokenized.cc`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/pw_log_zephyr_tokenized.cc;l\u003d56-81;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) takes `k_spin_lock(\u0026pw::log_zephyr::lock)`).\n2. Move [`console_log_notify_host()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console_buffer.c;l\u003d51-77;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) outside `console_lock` and gate **only** the host event notification on `k_can_yield()`:\n```c\nstatic void console_log_notify_host(void)\n{\n\tif (!k_can_yield())\n\t\treturn;\n\n\t/* Check wake_host (POWER_S0 / !usb_is_suspended()) ... */\n\tif (atomic_cas(\u0026new_console_log, 0, 1))\n\t\thost_set_single_event(EC_HOST_EVENT_CONSOLE_LOGS);\n}\n```\n\n### How this fixes the stack and avoids regressions\n1. **No dropped logs in non-yielding contexts**:\n   - [`pw_log_tokenized_HandleLog()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/pw_log_zephyr_tokenized.cc;l\u003d88-153;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745) works without dropping tokenized logs (`console_lock` nests cleanly inside `pw::log_zephyr::lock`).\n   - `PRE_KERNEL_1` / `PRE_KERNEL_2` logs (such as [`panic_data_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d372-442;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745)) are captured into `console_buf`, while `console_log_notify_host()` is safely skipped because `!k_can_yield()`.\n   - Logs from ISRs, `irq_lock()`, and the idle thread are all captured into `console_buf` instead of being dropped.\n2. **Makes https://crrev.com/c/8607950 ([`zephyr_print()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/console.c;l\u003d539-580;drc\u003d686b61c7c2fa3f6706c02a53762ba25f0bf69745)) and https://crrev.com/c/8607951 (`log_backend_cros_ec.c`) work for `!k_can_yield()` callers**:\n   - In `log_backend_cros_ec.c`, the `!k_can_yield()` path holds `k_spin_lock(\u0026isr_log_lock)` while calling `zephyr_print()`, which enters the `shell_stopped || !shell_is_active() || !k_can_yield()` branch and calls `console_buf_notify_chars(buff, size)`. With a spinlock in `console_buffer.c`, those logs (and `in_isr` logs if `console_buf_notify_chars()` is also called in the `in_isr` branch when `!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_LOG_MODE_MINIMAL)`) are actually recorded in `console_buf` instead of being discarded.",
      "revId": "6365158b1013805a36eaed1ee9949e51e0528891",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
